  "label": "Biological Sequence Model Validation",
  "related": [
    "fungal-calibrated-8715",
    "database-genome-3c30",
    "zero-dna-mirrordna-8a09"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "report-technical-4b00",
  "summary": "Five preprints test whether scores and benchmarks for co-folding, peptides, and perturbation models reflect the target property rather than artifacts.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is validation of whether model outputs and benchmark scores track the biological property of interest. Two antimicrobial peptide studies examine homology separation, length matching, cluster-disjoint versus random splitting, and negative-set choice; length alone separates classes under the first protocol. For protein-ligand co-folding, confidence scores barely outperform random selection, and a structural-agreement CORE Score is proposed as an alternative. The Virtual Cell Challenge 2026 metrics are calibrated on experimental repeats, and the closed-loop media design study shows that surrogate verifier accuracy metrics disagree on the next experiments, with conformal calibration addressing this. What is new is the shift from headline accuracy to reliability estimates and evaluation design that bear on downstream decisions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
